// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 184: Per-instance coverage of flow objects (page 253)
enum mode_e { M0, M1, M2 }
buffer b1 {
rand mode_e mode;
covergroup {
option.per_instance = true;
coverpoint mode;
} cs;
}
component pss_top {
pool b1 b1_p;
bind b1_p *;
action P_a {
output b1 b1_out;
}
action C_a {
input b1 b1_in;
}
action entry {
activity {
repeat (10) {
do C_a;
}
}
}
}

Also in Example 185, a contiguous path of named handles does not exist from the root action to the
covergroup instance inside the action traversal by type (do A). In this case, coverage data collected during
the 10 traversals of action A by type (do A) are placed in the per-type coverage collection associated with
covergroup type A::cg.
